From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] interconnect: qcom: sm8750: keep SN4 in the sleep set

SM8750 s2idle hangs on wake from a full CPU subsystem power collapse
(PSCI 0x200c354): no CPU returns from PSCI and the PMIC resets the board
about 90 s later. It happens whenever every vote on the SN4 BCM
(qns_pcie_mem_noc, the PCIe aggregate NoC to memory NoC link) is 0 in
the APPS sleep set, which is the case once the PCIe controller is
suspended.

Bisected with a debug sleep-set keepalive per BCM, PCIe floor removed:
MC0 alone, or MC0+SH0, still hangs; MC0+SH0+SN4 and SN4 alone resume.
With SN4 alone, MC0, SH0, ACV, CN0 and SN0 all drop to 0 in the sleep
set and the collapse still exits cleanly. The DDR vote is irrelevant;
the earlier PCIe suspend OPP floor only worked because its path
includes SN4. Turning the PCIe GDSCs fully off in suspend (upstream
PWRSTS_OFF_ON) does not avoid it.

Add keepalive_sleep to the BCM description: a BCM with it set keeps a
one-unit sleep-set vote whenever it would otherwise drop to 0. Set it
for SM8750's SN4.
---
diff --git a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/bcm-voter.c b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/bcm-voter.c
index 8e159cf..2bf4324 100644
--- a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/bcm-voter.c
+++ b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/bcm-voter.c
@@ -152,7 +152,8 @@ static void bcm_aggregate(struct qcom_icc_bcm *bcm)
 	}
 
 	if (bcm->vote_x[QCOM_ICC_BUCKET_SLEEP] == 0 &&
-	    bcm->vote_y[QCOM_ICC_BUCKET_SLEEP] == 0 && bcm_sleep_keepalive(bcm)) {
+	    bcm->vote_y[QCOM_ICC_BUCKET_SLEEP] == 0 &&
+	    (bcm->keepalive_sleep || bcm_sleep_keepalive(bcm))) {
 		bcm->vote_x[QCOM_ICC_BUCKET_SLEEP] = 1;
 		bcm->vote_y[QCOM_ICC_BUCKET_SLEEP] = 1;
 	}
diff --git a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpmh.h b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpmh.h
index 09d8791..1661d0c 100644
--- a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpmh.h
+++ b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpmh.h
@@ -118,6 +118,7 @@ struct qcom_icc_node {
  * @enable_mask: optional mask to send as vote instead of vote_x/vote_y
  * @dirty: flag used to indicate whether the bcm needs to be committed
  * @keepalive: flag used to indicate whether a keepalive is required
+ * @keepalive_sleep: also keep a minimal vote in the sleep set
  * @aux_data: auxiliary data used when calculating threshold values and
  * communicating with RPMh
  * @list: used to link to other bcms when compiling lists for commit
@@ -135,6 +136,7 @@ struct qcom_icc_bcm {
 	u32 enable_mask;
 	bool dirty;
 	bool keepalive;
+	bool keepalive_sleep;
 	struct bcm_db aux_data;
 	struct list_head list;
 	struct list_head ws_list;
diff --git a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/sm8750.c b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/sm8750.c
index 1486c0b..8141fad 100644
--- a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/sm8750.c
+++ b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/sm8750.c
@@ -1171,8 +1171,15 @@ static struct qcom_icc_bcm bcm_sn3 = {
 	.nodes = { &qnm_aggre2_noc },
 };
 
+/*
+ * The SoC fails to wake from a full CPU subsystem power collapse, and is
+ * reset, when this BCM is at 0 in the APPS sleep set. That happens whenever
+ * the PCIe controller is suspended, whatever the other DDR votes are. One
+ * unit is enough.
+ */
 static struct qcom_icc_bcm bcm_sn4 = {
 	.name = "SN4",
+	.keepalive_sleep = true,
 	.num_nodes = 1,
 	.nodes = { &qns_pcie_mem_noc },
 };
